WEBVTT

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:26.210
Saint Seiya

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.670
The Underworld.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.370
The land of the dead, ruled by Hades.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.910
A world without light.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:45.890
Young warriors of hope have entered
the Underworld in the name of peace.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.360
Yes, indeed.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.200
What's with all this rain?

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.090
I'm chilled to the bone, Seiya.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.470
If we remain wet, we'll freeze to death.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.290
Where's the Second Prison?

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.650
What's that?

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.780
This is the Second Prison.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.240
What's with the nasty smell?

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.670
What is that?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.340
What is this thing?

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:46.480
The Legendary Saint Orphée

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.840
Seiya.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.660
What a huge beast.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:06.170
What is this thing? Eating the
dead with its three heads.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.290
We don't have time to deal with that monster.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.670
Let's get out of here.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:16.580
It noticed us.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.300
Seiya!

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:31.770
Seiya.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.640
Seiya, get a hold of yourself. Seiya!

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.860
Did he not taste good, Cerberus?

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:50.540
No surprise. Those are Athena's Saints
who entered the Underworld alive.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.150
They must have tasted foul

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.380
compared to the dead you're used to eating.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.840
Who are you?

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.410
Of course.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:04.890
I am the guardian Specter of the
Second Prison, Sphinx Pharaoh.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:09.340
And this cute thing here is the
watchdog of hell, Cerberus.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.200
Sinners guilty of greed

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.870
are sent here to be devoured by Cerberus.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.810
The sin of greed?

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.580
You Saints have no fear
going up against Lord Hades.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.320
You're just food for Cerberus.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:36.380
Seiya!

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.900
Take this!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.400
Fool, that thin chain won't work on Cerberus.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:00.780
Seiya.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.130
Now you'll be eaten just like Pegasus.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:11.870
What?

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.920
I don't know what this thing is,

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.260
but we're Athena's Saints!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.140
What?

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.360
Watch out, Seiya.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.060
Great Capture!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.330
Cerberus!

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.380
It's all right. He just has a concussion.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.920
He'll wake up soon.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.560
Now, what are you going to do?

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.500
Do you also want a concussion?

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:08.470
Do you really want a curse from the Pharaoh?

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:14.390
You'll regret it. Being eaten
by Cerberus is the easy way out.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.610
Don't let your guard down, Shun.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:21.990
Hold on, Pharaoh.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.950
I'll be their opponent.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.650
What?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.100
Who are you?

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.350
Lyra Orphée.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.970
Orphée? I've heard of him.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.740
Me too.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:46.060
The legendary Silver Saint who is
more powerful than a Gold Saint.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.710
Lyra Orphée.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.490
Orphée's seductive harp

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.410
mesmerized the Pope

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.200
and the Gold Saints.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:16.680
The beautiful music is said
to have eased troubled minds.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.910
That legendary Saint is here.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:25.010
Why? Orphée suddenly went
missing a couple years ago.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.440
He was presumed dead.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:32.180
The fact that he's in the
Underworld must mean he's dead.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.870
No, you're wrong.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.310
Orphée is not dead.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:37.460
What?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.360
This man entered the Underworld alive

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.480
to serve Lord Hades.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.230
What?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:50.490
He willingly serves Hades as a Saint?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.290
Is that true, Orphée?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.140
Orphée, Athena is...

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.420
Shut up.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.600
No more questions.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.870
Now, die by a Pharaoh's spell.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.310
Balance of Curse!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.440
What is this intense sound?

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:22.310
It's so unpleasant. I've
never heard anything like it.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:30.560
I'm losing control of my body.
Just like what Pharaoh said.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.910
It really feels like I'm
being put under a spell.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.030
We're in trouble like this.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.440
Circle Defense!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:49.840
It's no use, you can't escape
the sound of my magic harp.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.830
No! The sound is penetrating my ears.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.610
Must... Stop...

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.410
Pegasus Meteor Punch!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.740
Damn. It didn't work at all.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.690
My body is getting heavy.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.400
That's right, you're already under my spell.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.910
Look at the changes to your body.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.380
What?

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:20.920
Seiya.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.650
What is this?

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.560
My heart. My heart!

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:37.470
Yes, your heart will be
weighed on the sacred scale.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.600
If it doesn't balance evenly
with the feather of the Ma'ato,

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.270
the symbol of truth,

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:46.070
you will be deemed evil.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.970
And not only your body, but
your soul will be obliterated.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:53.960
Seiya.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.850
Now, heart of Pegasus,

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.160
leave his body and get on the sacred scale.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.220
What? My heart is back to normal.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.190
Seiya.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.820
What happened?

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:38.190
Orphée, why do you interrupt?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.580
Orphée, are you...

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:41.700
Could it be?

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:46.240
The legendary attack of Lyra Orphée's harp?

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.150
Stringer Nocturne.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.400
Orphée.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:07.140
I told you I'll be their opponent,

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.140
and both of them are finished.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.230
There's nothing to complain about.

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:33.590
Eurydice, I'm sorry to leave you
alone. You must have been lonely.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.110
Seiya.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:48.990
Seiya.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.630
Wake up, Seiya.

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:55.010
Shun.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:56.690
Shun.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.750
Wake up, Shun.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.410
Athena.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:06.580
Brother.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.480
Are you all right, Shun?

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:12.650
Yes, but my body is still numb.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:16.810
We are both still alive.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.830
But where are we?

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:21.450
Flower petals.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.370
How is this possible in the Underworld?

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.300
Seiya, look at that.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:37.880
She's turning into stone,
but she's so beautiful.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.320
Why would such a beautiful
woman like her be like this?

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:43.880
Who is it?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.860
You're alive.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:49.400
Who are you?

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:53.290
We are Athena's Saints.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:58.780
Saints? Are you really Athena's Saints?

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.330
Yes.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:05.060
I'm glad, I mean, I'm very happy.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:11.690
I've been waiting a long
time for this day to come.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.640
You were waiting for us?

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:17.730
Yes, I beg you, young Saints.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.860
Somehow, somehow help Orphée.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.080
Help?

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:28.320
Yes, he... Because of me... Because of me...

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:34.340
What happened? Why are you in the Underworld?

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.230
Well...

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:44.480
As you know, Orphée and I
were living above on earth.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.290
I loved Orphée, one of Athena's Saints.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:53.550
And in turn, Orphée loved me.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:59.420
We were very happy.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:07.140
Orphée, please be by my side forever.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:11.180
I want to listen to your harp forever.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:15.230
Eurydice, I will forever be by your side.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.370
And I will continue to play the harp for you.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:22.880
And if you die, I'll play for ever.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:24.030
Orphée.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.970
However, a dark fate awaited us.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:43.870
I died by the bite of a poisonous snake.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.380
Eurydice.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:50.880
Orphée decided to go to the Underworld

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:58.470
to ask Hades to return my soul to Earth.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:05.920
Orphée played his harp in front of Hades.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:12.890
It was very beautiful and full of melancholy.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:18.250
Lord Hades, I don't care
what happens to my body.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:23.050
Will you please return
Eurydice's soul to Earth?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:29.040
In return, I will play my harp for
you in the Underworld forever.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:38.280
Orphée, Lord Hades seems
to be fond of your harp.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:45.310
As a reward, he is going to
return Eurydice's soul to Earth.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:47.240
Really?

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:50.460
The Lord of the Underworld doesn't lie.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.710
Orphée.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.480
Eurydice.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.040
Orphée.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:58.470
Eurydice.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:07.300
Please tell Lord Hades I
will never forget this.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:11.050
Orphée, I'll warn you about one thing.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.150
Until you get back to Earth,

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:17.820
you must never look back.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.810
If you look back even once,

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:25.580
your wish will not be granted.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:31.510
Such music that Lord Hades is delighted with

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:35.270
would be a shame to go back to Earth.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:39.720
Is there any way to lure back Orphée?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:44.040
Then Lord Hades can listen to that music

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.970
whenever he pleases.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.540
Pharaoh.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:50.230
Yes.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:55.270
We can't set a precedent by
letting the dead return to Earth.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:57.690
Don't let Orphée return to Earth.

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:01.900
Stop him at your Second Prison.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.860
Understand?

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:04.570
Yes.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.550
Eurydice, just a little further,
the exit to Earth is not far.

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:19.030
I'm happy, Orphée, to be able to
hear your beautiful music on Earth.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:22.620
That's right. We're almost there.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.570
What's that light?

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.240
It's the light from Earth.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.740
We've finally arrived at the exit to Earth.

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:43.750
Eurydice, look, it's sunlight.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:53.210
Eurydice.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.400
Orphée.

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:03.680
Eurydice.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.320
No way.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.660
So then, Orphée...

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:13.710
Yes, he decided to stay here
and play the harp for me.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:16.500
To keep his promise with me.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:18.460
However,

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:22.330
I can no longer return to Earth.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:27.140
Please, at least take Orphée back to Earth.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:31.570
He's kept me company long enough.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.290
Please take him back to Earth by all means.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.080
Please. I beg you.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.620
How sad.

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:45.270
Do people have to suffer even for love?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:50.230
But why did Orphée think it was sunlight?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.200
If it wasn't for that, they would
have made it back to Earth.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.570
Orphée.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:10.220
Why won't you flee now that
you've regained consciousness?

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:14.130
I spared your lives because you are Saints.

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:16.760
I knew you were easy on us.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:22.370
I'll let you know, you can't
defeat Lord Hades at your level.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.220
If you value your lives,

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.560
leave immediately.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:32.560
We can't. Athena is headed
towards Hades alone right now.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.520
She needs protection or she'll be killed,

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:42.150
so we need to get this Cloth to her quickly.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.910
So what's your point?

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:52.850
What do you mean? If Athena dies,

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.880
there's no one who can defeat Hades.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.160
The Earth will belong to Hades

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:03.300
and people will suffer
a living hell, Orphée.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.380
Of all people, you should understand that.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:10.180
There's no guarantee Earth
will become a living hell.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.630
The world can be cleansed
and a utopia realized.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.140
What do you mean?

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:24.140
Lord Hades is not who you think he is.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:29.450
And as you've heard, I am indebted to him.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.170
So be quiet and leave.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.880
I know how much you love Eurydice.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.000
But...

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:42.230
Enough, Shun. No point trying
to convince a traitor.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:44.290
This man is no longer a Saint.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:46.860
He sold his soul to Hades.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:51.770
We don't have the time to
deal with him. Let's go.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:52.770
Seiya.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.580
Forget it. Let's hurry.

00:20:58.710 --> 00:20:59.710
Orphée.

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:03.310
What's that light?

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:07.240
I didn't think I'd see such
a light in the Underworld.

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.280
Orphée, is that...

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:13.990
Yes, it's the same light
I mistook for the sun.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:17.180
Athena's Cloth!

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:21.490
Seiya.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.360
So this is Athena's Cloth.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:31.970
Who knew the Bronze Saints
carried such valuables?

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:36.390
I'll take it to Miss Pandora.
She will be pleased.

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:38.850
Give it back!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:43.020
Don't move! You know you can't beat me.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:44.570
What?

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:46.490
Orphée.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:51.670
You said you finished them off.

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.710
What's going on?

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:59.770
As suspected, you're still
on the side of the Saints.

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:01.670
Tell me one thing.

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:07.510
That time, was it you who
created the light I saw?

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.090
If so, what will you do about it?

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:12.300
What will I do?

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:15.850
You ask what will I do?

00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:23.360
It's obvious.

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:28.060
This will become your grave.

00:24:04.350 --> 00:24:07.700
The legendary Saint, Orphée finally reappears.

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:09.540
When he learns the truth,

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:13.230
his lyre starts playing a beautiful
song of determination.

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:17.460
Is the melody that resonates in the
Underworld filled with hope or despair?

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:21.350
Orphée, I know what you want me to do.

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:24.920
Saint Seiya: "Orphée, The Sad Requiem."

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.020
Have you ever felt your Cosmo?
